    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 430 of 2012",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2907\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 430 of the laws of 2012 relating\nto a certain agreement for a payment in lieu of taxes, in relation to\nthe effectiveness thereof\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: The bill clarifies that the provisions\nof L. 2012, c. 430 are only applicable for taxable years 2008 through\n2012.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: This legislation is needed to ensure that a leased prop-\nerty in the City of Poughkeepsie that was granted a qualifying empire\nzone enterprise is not unduly burdened with unexpected tax obligations\nas a result of \"reach back\" due to a change in policy by the New York\nState Department of Taxation and Finance.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE: None\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: Effective immediately,\n\n",
